Execution:
1. [task] Which finding is in this chest X-ray?
Options: {"A": "small right pleural effusion", "B": "small left pleural effusion"}
2. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"chest_xray_expert","args":{"question":"Is there evidence of a pleural effusion in this lateral chest X-ray? If so, describe the location and laterality based on anatomical landmarks."}}],"reason":"Determine presence and laterality of pleural effusion using expert analysis of lateral view"}
3. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"llava_med_qa","args":{"question":"On this lateral chest X-ray, is there blunting of the posterior costophrenic angle or increased opacity in the lower posterior lung field suggesting a pleural effusion? If present, which side is more likely affected based on typical lateral view anatomy?"}}],"reason":"Cross-validate expert finding with another model focused on posterior costophrenic angle and lower lung opacity"}
4. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"roi_crop","args":{"box":[0.3,0.6,1.0,1.0],"zoom":2}}],"reason":"Zoom into posterior costophrenic angles on lateral view to visually assess for blunting/effusion and confirm laterality"}
5. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"medvlm_r1","args":{"question":"On this lateral chest X-ray, is there blunting of the posterior costophrenic angle or increased opacity in the lower posterior lung field suggesting a pleural effusion? If present, which side is more likely affected based on typical lateral view anatomy?"}}],"reason":"Obtain independent third-model assessment of posterior costophrenic angle and laterality to resolve conflict between prior tools"}
6. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"llava_rad","args":{"question":"Does this lateral chest X-ray show blunting of the posterior costophrenic angle or increased opacity in the lower posterior lung field suggesting a pleural effusion? If present, which side is more likely affected based on typical lateral view anatomy?"}}],"reason":"Obtain fourth independent model assessment to resolve conflicting evidence and confirm laterality"}
7. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"verify","args":{"proposed_answer":"B. small left pleural effusion","risk":"Conflicting tool outputs: chest_xray_expert says no effusion, llava_med_qa says left effusion, llava_rad confirms pleural fluid in major fissure without specifying side; need audit to resolve laterality and presence before finalizing."}}],"reason":"Audit conflicting evidence on presence and laterality of pleural effusion before committing to answer"}
8. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"medgemma","args":{"question":"On this lateral chest X-ray, is there blunting of the posterior costophrenic angle or increased opacity in the lower posterior lung field suggesting a pleural effusion? If present, which side is more likely affected based on typical lateral view anatomy?"}}],"reason":"Obtain additional independent model assessment to weigh against verifier's caution and resolve laterality"}
9. [action] {"answer":"B. small left pleural effusion","reason":"llava_med_qa identified blunting of the posterior costophrenic angle and increased opacity suggestive of a left-sided pleural effusion, while other models were inconclusive or failed to specify laterality."}
10. [released_benchmark_feedback] Historical reference: B. small left pleural effusion

